      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COUSR00C USER LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COUSR00C's user-list browse CICS transaction by
      *  mocking ONLY the program's external boundary into the CICS
      *  API: the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS translator
      *  emits in place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE MAP, SEND
      *  MAP, STARTBR DATASET (USRSEC), READNEXT DATASET, READPREV
      *  DATASET, ENDBR DATASET, XCTL, RETURN).  The DFHEI1 entry
      *  point is the single ABI seam between the production COBOL
      *  program and the CICS runtime; mocking it intercepts every
      *  CICS service call without requiring a live CICS region or
      *  a populated USRSEC VSAM cluster.
      *
      *  Internal COUSR00C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every
      *  TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM
      *  so the testsuite asserts against side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per the user directive in AAP
      *  Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS
      *  -------------------------------------------
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser supports the mock-types
      *  CALL, PARA, PARAGRAPH, and SECTION (verified against the
      *  Keywords class in cobol-check-0.2.16.jar).  At link time on
      *  z/OS the CICS translator (DFHECP1$) rewrites every
      *      EXEC CICS <verb> ... END-EXEC.
      *  into a sequence whose terminal statement is
      *      CALL 'DFHEI1' USING <command-block> ...
      *  so MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is the equivalent intercept point.
      *  Off-platform (GnuCOBOL on Linux) the same mock applies once
      *  the CICS translator runs as a precompile pass; until that
      *  pass exists the merged binary fails to compile (a known
      *  infrastructure gap covered by AAP Section 6.6.3.1's
      *  documented "manual testing only" baseline) and the mock
      *  simply registers without firing.  The testsuite is
      *  forward-compatible: when a CICS translator pass is added,
      *  the same .cut file exercises every CICS boundary through
      *  this mock.
      *
      *  Mock placement rule
      *  -------------------
      *  Each MOCK is declared INSIDE its corresponding TESTCASE
      *  block (after the TESTCASE keyword) so the cobol-check parser
      *  binds the mock's Local scope to the CURRENT testcase name.
      *  Mirrors the exemplar pattern in COUSR03C.cut, COUSR02C.cut,
      *  and COUSR01C.cut.
      *
      *  Schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl)
      *  -----------------------------------------------------
      *  The file_schema names two internal imports:
      *
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy -- 01-level EXTERNAL
      *        working-storage group used by the CEE3ABD and DFHEI1
      *        link-time stubs to publish abend / unmocked-CICS
      *        flags to the testsuite.
      *
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl -- standalone DFHEI1 PROGRAM-ID
      *        compiled into a .so module so that any unmocked
      *        EXEC CICS verb that survives the off-platform compile
      *        resolves at load time (CICS NOT-AUTH 27).
      *
      *  Both stubs are linked at TEST-RUN time by the runner script
      *  tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_run_tests.  The
      *  testsuite itself does NOT contain `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.`
      *  because cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser only recognizes
      *  the keywords TESTSUITE, TESTCASE, MOCK, EXPECT, VERIFY,
      *  BEFORE-EACH, AFTER-EACH, END-BEFORE, END-AFTER, END-MOCK,
      *  CALL, PARA, PARAGRAPH, SECTION (and assertion connectors
      *  TO BE / TO EQUAL / HAPPENED / TIMES / AT LEAST / etc).  A
      *  bare COPY at file scope is parsed as a fieldname token and
      *  triggers a "Unexpected token" SYNTAX ERROR that aborts
      *  cobol-check before it can merge the testsuite into the
      *  production source.  The COUSR03C / COUSR02C / COUSR01C
      *  exemplars (the canonical pattern per AAP Section 0.4.3 and
      *  the user prompt) follow the same omission.  The runtime
      *  stubs satisfy the link-time requirements without WS access
      *  from the .cut file (DFHEI1 NOT-AUTH fallback, CEE3ABD
      *  GOBACK-with-flag).
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
      *          = SPACES; production substitutes the default
      *          'COSGN00C' target, captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields,
      *          and issues XCTL.  This is the PF3 / initial-entry
      *          path (production lines 110-112 set the EIBCALEN=0
      *          default; lines 125-127 set it on PF3).
      *    TC2 - PERFORM INITIALIZE-USER-DATA with WS-IDX=1;
      *          production EVALUATE WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1
      *          clause (lines 449-453) and clears USRID01I, FNAME01I,
      *          LNAME01I, UTYPE01I to SPACES.  No CICS verbs;
      *          purely WORKING-STORAGE side effects.
      *    TC3 - PERFORM POPULATE-USER-DATA with WS-IDX=1 and
      *          SEC-USER-DATA pre-populated; production EVALUATE
      *          WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1 clause (lines 387-392)
      *          and copies SEC-USR-* into row-1 BMS fields.  The
      *          WHEN 1 branch ALSO copies SEC-USR-ID into
      *          CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST (line 389) -- the COMMAREA
      *          "first user on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF7-KEY
      *          reads (line 242) for backward paging.
      *    TC4 - PERFORM POPULATE-USER-DATA with WS-IDX=10; matches
      *          the WHEN 10 clause (lines 433-438) which copies
      *          SEC-USR-ID into CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST (line 435) --
      *          the "last user on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF8-KEY
      *          reads (line 265) for forward paging.  TC3 and TC4
      *          form differential coverage of the row-1 / row-10
      *          slices and their unique anchor MOVEs.
      *    TC5 - PERFORM PROCESS-PF7-KEY with CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM=1;
      *          production lines 248-255 take the ELSE branch of
      *          the IF CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM > 1 guard, setting
      *          WS-MESSAGE to the "top of the page" advisory and
      *          flipping WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG to 'N' before performing
      *          SEND-USRLST-SCREEN.  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
      *          intercepts SEND-USRLST-SCREEN's EXEC CICS SEND.
      *    TC6 - PERFORM PROCESS-PF8-KEY with CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-
      *          FLG NOT = 'Y'; production lines 270-277 take the
      *          ELSE branch of the IF NEXT-PAGE-YES guard, setting
      *          WS-MESSAGE to the "bottom of the page" advisory.
      *          TC5 and TC6 form symmetric coverage of the two
      *          paging-boundary advisory paths.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  Per AAP Section 0.10.2 and the user prompt, only ADMIN001 /
      *  ADMIN role is permitted in the COUSR00C testsuite (this
      *  transaction is admin-gated upstream by COADM01C; non-admin
      *  access is filtered before the user reaches COUSR00C, so the
      *  program itself does not implement role-based authorization
      *  and therefore has no test surface for a "non-admin attempting
      *  access rejected" case as the user-prompt TC2 stub would
      *  imply -- the rejection occurs in COADM01C, not COUSR00C, so
      *  the TC2 slot is repurposed to the INITIALIZE-USER-DATA
      *  WS-only test described above, mirroring COUSR02C and
      *  COUSR03C which made the identical repurposing decision).
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 -- user directive on test structure
      *    AAP Section 0.5.1  -- file-by-file plan for COUSR00C
      *    AAP Section 0.10.2 -- ADMIN001 / ADMIN test user
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 098-144 (MAIN-PARA)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 237-255 (PROCESS-PF7-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 260-277 (PROCESS-PF8-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 384-441 (POPULATE-USER-DATA)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 446-501 (INITIALIZE-USER-DATA)
      *    app/cbl/COUSR00C.cbl lines 506-517 (RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy            (SEC-USER-DATA layout)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COUSR00.CPY         (COUSR0AI / COUSR0AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR03C.cut  (canonical exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR02C.cut  (sister CRUD exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR01C.cut  (sister CRUD exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'COUSR00C USER LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE starts
      *  from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check resets
      *  MOCK invocation counters automatically between TESTCASEs;
      *  this block resets the application working-storage groups the
      *  production code reads or writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        - WS-PGMNAME, WS-TRANID, WS-USRSEC-FILE,
      *                          WS-ERR-FLG, WS-USER-SEC-EOF,
      *                          WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG, WS-RESP-CD,
      *                          WS-REAS-CD, WS-REC-COUNT, WS-IDX,
      *                          WS-PAGE-NUM, WS-MESSAGE (production
      *                          lines 35-54).  After INITIALIZE,
      *                          GnuCOBOL re-applies VALUE clauses so
      *                          WS-PGMNAME='COUSR00C', WS-TRANID=
      *                          'CU00', WS-USRSEC-FILE='USRSEC  '.
      *    WS-USER-DATA        - 10-occurrence USER-REC table.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   - whole COCOM01Y group plus the
      *                          CDEMO-CU00-INFO extension fields
      *                          (USRID-FIRST/LAST, PAGE-NUM,
      *                           NEXT-PAGE-FLG, USR-SEL-FLG,
      *                           USR-SELECTED).
      *    SEC-USER-DATA       - CSUSR01Y group (SEC-USR-ID,
      *                          SEC-USR-FNAME, SEC-USR-LNAME,
      *                          SEC-USR-PWD, SEC-USR-TYPE,
      *                          SEC-USR-FILLER) -- the buffer that
      *                          READNEXT-USER-SEC-FILE writes via
      *                          INTO(SEC-USER-DATA), and that
      *                          POPULATE-USER-DATA reads to fill
      *                          the BMS map.
      *    COUSR0AI            - BMS input map (USRIDINI, SEL0001I..
      *                          SEL0010I, USRID01I..USRID10I,
      *                          FNAME/LNAME/UTYPE row fields,
      *                          PAGENUMI, ERRMSGI).
      *    RETURN-CODE         - implicit special register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  ADMIN001 admin-role identity (the only test user permitted
      *  by AAP Section 0.10.2 for this transaction) so each TESTCASE
      *  starts from the routed-by-COADM01C state that production
      *  COUSR00C expects.  CDEMO-FROM-* fields default to the
      *  upstream admin menu so RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN has a non-empty
      *  origin to reflect back into the COMMAREA before XCTL.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE WS-USER-DATA
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE SEC-USER-DATA
            INITIALIZE COUSR0AI
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'ADMIN001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'A'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COADM01C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CA00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN (production lines 506-517).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3
      *  branch (production lines 125-127) and of the EIBCALEN = 0
      *  initial-entry branch (production lines 110-112).  The
      *  paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES         (line 508)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM            (line 509)
      *    END-IF
      *    MOVE WS-TRANID    TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID             (line 511)
      *    MOVE WS-PGMNAME   TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM            (line 512)
      *    MOVE ZEROS        TO CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT             (line 513)
      *    EXEC CICS                                          (line 514)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                 (line 515)
      *        COMMAREA(CARDDEMO-COMMAREA)                    (line 516)
      *    END-EXEC.                                          (line 517)
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC1 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in
      *                       BEFORE-EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X
      *                       group fills with spaces, satisfying
      *                       the WHEN OR SPACES half of the
      *                       line-508 IF).
      *    CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM = 'COADM01C' (BEFORE-EACH default;
      *                       will be overwritten by line-512
      *                       production MOVE -- the test asserts
      *                       the SIDE EFFECT)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 509 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic)
      *    'COUSR00C' - WS-PGMNAME constant declared at production
      *                 line 36 (PIC X(08) VALUE 'COUSR00C'); MOVE'd
      *                 to CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM by line 512
      *    'CU00'     - WS-TRANID constant declared at production
      *                 line 37 (PIC X(04) VALUE 'CU00'); MOVE'd to
      *                 CDEMO-FROM-TRANID by line 511
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COUSR00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CU00'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- INITIALIZE-USER-DATA clears row 1 BMS fields
      *
      *  Drives INITIALIZE-USER-DATA (production lines 446-501) with
      *  WS-IDX = 1.  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs
      *  and zero PERFORM statements; it is the cleanest test target
      *  in COUSR00C.  The EVALUATE WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1 clause
      *  and executes:
      *
      *    MOVE SPACES TO USRID01I OF COUSR0AI                (line 450)
      *    MOVE SPACES TO FNAME01I OF COUSR0AI                (line 451)
      *    MOVE SPACES TO LNAME01I OF COUSR0AI                (line 452)
      *    MOVE SPACES TO UTYPE01I OF COUSR0AI                (line 453)
      *
      *  Invoked from PROCESS-PAGE-FORWARD (line 294) and
      *  PROCESS-PAGE-BACKWARD (line 348) inside a PERFORM VARYING
      *  WS-IDX FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-IDX > 10 loop to reset the
      *  entire 10-row BMS table before a fresh page render.  Testing
      *  WS-IDX=1 covers the row-1 slice of that loop.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude (after BEFORE-EACH
      *  zeroes the structures): seed USRID01I / FNAME01I / LNAME01I
      *  / UTYPE01I with non-empty markers so the test proves the
      *  production MOVE TO SPACES actually overwrites them.  Without
      *  these seeds the BEFORE-EACH initial state would already be
      *  SPACES and the test would not distinguish the production
      *  paragraph's effect from baseline.  Set WS-IDX=1 to drive
      *  the EVALUATE to the WHEN 1 clause.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    SPACES - production literal MOVE'd by lines 450-453;
      *             the test asserts the side effect (does NOT
      *             reimplement the MOVE)
      *
      *  A MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is declared so the testcase can also
      *  ASSERT (via VERIFY ... HAPPENED 0 TIMES) the production
      *  invariant that INITIALIZE-USER-DATA NEVER reaches a CICS
      *  service call.  A regression that introduces an EXEC CICS
      *  verb inside this paragraph would inflate the mock count
      *  and fail the VERIFY clause.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C INITIALIZE-USER-DATA clears row 1 fields'
            MOVE 'OLDUSR01' TO USRID01I OF COUSR0AI
            MOVE 'OLDFNAME01          ' TO FNAME01I OF COUSR0AI
            MOVE 'OLDLNAME01          ' TO LNAME01I OF COUSR0AI
            MOVE 'X' TO UTYPE01I OF COUSR0AI
            MOVE 1 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM INITIALIZE-USER-DATA
            EXPECT USRID01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT FNAME01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT LNAME01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE SPACES
            EXPECT UTYPE01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE SPACES
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- POPULATE-USER-DATA fills row 1 + sets FIRST anchor
      *
      *  Drives POPULATE-USER-DATA (production lines 384-441) with
      *  WS-IDX = 1 and SEC-USER-DATA pre-populated with a fixture
      *  user record.  The paragraph contains zero EXEC CICS verbs;
      *  the EVALUATE WS-IDX matches the WHEN 1 clause and executes:
      *
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-ID    TO USRID01I OF COUSR0AI         (line 388)
      *                          CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST       (line 389)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-FNAME TO FNAME01I OF COUSR0AI         (line 390)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-LNAME TO LNAME01I OF COUSR0AI         (line 391)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-TYPE  TO UTYPE01I OF COUSR0AI         (line 392)
      *
      *  The line-389 destination CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST is the
      *  COMMAREA "first user on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF7-KEY
      *  reads at line 242 to seed SEC-USR-ID for the next backward
      *  STARTBR.  The test asserts both the per-row map move
      *  (USRID01I .. UTYPE01I) AND the anchor side effect, so a
      *  regression that drops EITHER of the two destinations of
      *  the line-388 MOVE TO is caught by exactly one of the two
      *  corresponding EXPECT clauses.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC3 prelude:
      *    SEC-USR-ID    = 'USER0001'                  (8-byte literal)
      *    SEC-USR-FNAME = 'Alice               '      (20-byte padded)
      *    SEC-USR-LNAME = 'Tester              '      (20-byte padded)
      *    SEC-USR-TYPE  = 'U'                         (1-byte literal)
      *    WS-IDX        = 1
      *
      *  Source of expected values: all four are test fixtures set
      *  in the TC3 prelude; production lines 388/390/391/392 MOVE
      *  them into the BMS map; production line 389 ALSO MOVEs
      *  SEC-USR-ID into CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C POPULATE-USER-DATA row 1 sets USRID-FIRST'
            MOVE 'USER0001'             TO SEC-USR-ID
            MOVE 'Alice               ' TO SEC-USR-FNAME
            MOVE 'Tester              ' TO SEC-USR-LNAME
            MOVE 'U'                    TO SEC-USR-TYPE
            MOVE 1 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-USER-DATA
            EXPECT USRID01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'USER0001'
            EXPECT FNAME01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'Alice               '
            EXPECT LNAME01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'Tester              '
            EXPECT UTYPE01I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'U'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST TO BE 'USER0001'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- POPULATE-USER-DATA fills row 10 + sets LAST anchor
      *
      *  Drives POPULATE-USER-DATA (production lines 384-441) with
      *  WS-IDX = 10 and SEC-USER-DATA pre-populated with a fixture
      *  user record.  The EVALUATE WS-IDX matches the WHEN 10
      *  clause and executes:
      *
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-ID    TO USRID10I OF COUSR0AI         (line 434)
      *                          CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST        (line 435)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-FNAME TO FNAME10I OF COUSR0AI         (line 436)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-LNAME TO LNAME10I OF COUSR0AI         (line 437)
      *    MOVE SEC-USR-TYPE  TO UTYPE10I OF COUSR0AI         (line 438)
      *
      *  The line-435 destination CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST is the
      *  COMMAREA "last user on page" anchor that PROCESS-PF8-KEY
      *  reads at line 265 to seed SEC-USR-ID for the next forward
      *  STARTBR.  TC3 and TC4 form differential coverage: TC3
      *  covers the row-1 slice and the FIRST anchor; TC4 covers
      *  the row-10 slice and the LAST anchor.  Each anchor is
      *  unique to exactly one EVALUATE clause, so a regression
      *  that drops the FIRST or LAST anchor MOVE is caught by
      *  exactly one of the two tests.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC4 prelude:
      *    SEC-USR-ID    = 'USER0050'                  (8-byte literal)
      *    SEC-USR-FNAME = 'Zara                '      (20-byte padded)
      *    SEC-USR-LNAME = 'Reviewer            '      (20-byte padded)
      *    SEC-USR-TYPE  = 'A'                         (1-byte literal)
      *    WS-IDX        = 10
      *
      *  Source of expected values: all four are test fixtures set
      *  in the TC4 prelude; production lines 434/436/437/438 MOVE
      *  them into the BMS map; production line 435 ALSO MOVEs
      *  SEC-USR-ID into CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C POPULATE-USER-DATA row 10 sets USRID-LAST'
            MOVE 'USER0050'             TO SEC-USR-ID
            MOVE 'Zara                ' TO SEC-USR-FNAME
            MOVE 'Reviewer            ' TO SEC-USR-LNAME
            MOVE 'A'                    TO SEC-USR-TYPE
            MOVE 10 TO WS-IDX
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM POPULATE-USER-DATA
            EXPECT USRID10I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'USER0050'
            EXPECT FNAME10I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'Zara                '
            EXPECT LNAME10I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'Reviewer            '
            EXPECT UTYPE10I OF COUSR0AI TO BE 'A'
            EXPECT CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST TO BE 'USER0050'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- PROCESS-PF7-KEY at page 1 sets top-of-page advisory
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-PF7-KEY (production lines 237-255) with
      *  CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM = 1 (current page is the first page).
      *  Production lines 248-255 execute the ELSE branch of the
      *  IF CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM > 1 guard, which encodes the
      *  production-mandated invariant: a backward-paging request
      *  from page 1 has no valid prior page, so the program must
      *  surface a user-visible advisory rather than issue a doomed
      *  READPREV that would return NOTFND from before the first
      *  record.  The ELSE branch executes:
      *
      *    MOVE 'You are already at the top of the page...' TO
      *                    WS-MESSAGE                        (line 251)
      *    SET SEND-ERASE-NO TO TRUE                         (line 253)
      *    PERFORM SEND-USRLST-SCREEN                        (line 254)
      *
      *  The two preludes the production paragraph executes BEFORE
      *  reaching the IF guard are also exercised:
      *    Line 245: SET NEXT-PAGE-YES TO TRUE
      *              (CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG = 'Y')
      *    Line 246: MOVE -1 TO USRIDINL OF COUSR0AI
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC5 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST = 'USER0010'  (non-empty so the
      *                            IF at line 239 takes the ELSE
      *                            branch and MOVEs to SEC-USR-ID
      *                            via line 242)
      *    CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM    = 1           (so line 248 IF
      *                            > 1 is FALSE and the ELSE
      *                            branch is taken)
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'You are already at the top of the page...'
      *                            - production literal MOVE'd by
      *                              line 251-252 (test asserts the
      *                              side effect)
      *    'N'                     - SEND-ERASE-NO 88-level value
      *                              (production line 48 declares
      *                              the 88; line 253 SETs the
      *                              parent flag to 'N')
      *    -1                      - USRIDINL flipped by line 246
      *    'Y'                     - NEXT-PAGE-YES 88-level value
      *                              (production line 72 declares
      *                              the 88; line 245 SETs the
      *                              parent flag to 'Y')
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts SEND-USRLST-SCREEN's
      *  EXEC CICS SEND verb (after CICS translator rewrite) so no
      *  3270 traffic is generated.  The VERIFY clause asserts the
      *  LOW BOUND on the mock invocation count.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C PROCESS-PF7-KEY at top sets top-of-page msg'
            MOVE 'USER0010' TO CDEMO-CU00-USRID-FIRST
            MOVE 1 TO CDEMO-CU00-PAGE-NUM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-PF7-KEY
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE 'You are already at the top of the page...'
            EXPECT WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT USRIDINL OF COUSR0AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- PROCESS-PF8-KEY at bottom sets bottom-of-page advisory
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-PF8-KEY (production lines 260-277) with
      *  CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG NOT = 'Y' (no next page available;
      *  the 88-level NEXT-PAGE-YES is FALSE so the IF at line 270
      *  takes the ELSE branch).  Production lines 273-277 execute
      *  the ELSE branch, which encodes the dual of TC5's invariant:
      *  a forward-paging request when no further records remain
      *  has no valid next page, so the program surfaces a
      *  user-visible advisory rather than issue a doomed READNEXT
      *  that would return ENDFILE.  The ELSE branch executes:
      *
      *    MOVE 'You are already at the bottom of the page...' TO
      *                    WS-MESSAGE                        (line 273)
      *    SET SEND-ERASE-NO TO TRUE                         (line 275)
      *    PERFORM SEND-USRLST-SCREEN                        (line 276)
      *
      *  The two preludes the production paragraph executes BEFORE
      *  reaching the IF guard are also exercised:
      *    Line 265: MOVE CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST TO SEC-USR-ID
      *              (since CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST is set in the
      *              TC6 prelude and is therefore not SPACES /
      *              LOW-VALUES, the IF at line 262 takes the
      *              ELSE branch and MOVEs the anchor)
      *    Line 268: MOVE -1 TO USRIDINL OF COUSR0AI
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC6 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST = 'USER0050'   (non-empty so the
      *                            IF at line 262 takes the ELSE
      *                            branch and MOVEs the anchor to
      *                            SEC-USR-ID via line 265)
      *    CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG = SPACES    (set by INITIALIZE
      *                            in BEFORE-EACH; the 88-level
      *                            NEXT-PAGE-YES checks for 'Y'
      *                            which SPACES is not, so the
      *                            ELSE branch at line 272 is
      *                            taken).  Explicitly RE-MOVED
      *                            here as SPACES to make the
      *                            test author's intent obvious.
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'You are already at the bottom of the page...'
      *                            - production literal MOVE'd by
      *                              line 273-274 (test asserts
      *                              the side effect)
      *    'N'                     - SEND-ERASE-NO 88-level value
      *                              (line 275 SETs to 'N')
      *    -1                      - USRIDINL flipped by line 268
      *    'USER0050'              - test fixture set in TC6 prelude
      *                              and copied to SEC-USR-ID by
      *                              production line 265
      *
      *  TC5 and TC6 form symmetric coverage of the two paging-
      *  boundary advisory paths.  A regression that swaps the PF7
      *  and PF8 advisory branches (e.g., copy-paste error in the
      *  production source) is caught by both tests failing
      *  simultaneously with mismatched WS-MESSAGE values.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COUSR00C PROCESS-PF8-KEY at end sets bottom-of-page msg'
            MOVE 'USER0050' TO CDEMO-CU00-USRID-LAST
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-CU00-NEXT-PAGE-FLG
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-PF8-KEY
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE 'You are already at the bottom of the page...'
            EXPECT WS-SEND-ERASE-FLG TO BE 'N'
            EXPECT USRIDINL OF COUSR0AI NOT = 0
            EXPECT SEC-USR-ID TO BE 'USER0050'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED AT LEAST 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COUSR00C USER LIST BROWSE TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************
